This program uses ARMv7-A Thumb instructions.

Name register zero "address of the next entry".
Name register one "number of entries remaining".
Name register two "running total".
Name register three "current entry".
Name register twelve "unknown marker".

Name the following instruction "prepare the total".
Put zero into "running total" without changing the condition flags.
Put 65535 into the low sixteen bits of "unknown marker" and zero into its high sixteen bits.
Put 65535 into the high sixteen bits of "unknown marker" without changing its low sixteen bits.

Name the following instruction "check whether any entries remain".
Compare "number of entries remaining" with zero and update the condition flags.
If the zero flag is one, replace the execution index with the instruction named "return the result".
Load exactly four bytes from the address in "address of the next entry" into "current entry".
Increase "address of the next entry" by four without changing the condition flags.
Decrease "number of entries remaining" by one without changing the condition flags.
Compare "current entry" with "unknown marker" and update the condition flags.
If the zero flag is one, replace the execution index with the instruction named "check whether any entries remain".
Add "current entry" to "running total" and keep only the lowest thirty-two result bits without changing the condition flags.
Replace the execution index with the instruction named "check whether any entries remain".

Name the following instruction "return the result".
Copy "running total" into "address of the next entry" without changing the condition flags.
Replace the execution index with the instruction address in the link register.
